# DESKTOP_INSTALL_PROBE.hss

## Program
Linux Desktop Install Probe

## Purpose
Small native helper that discovers the repository clone, locates the primed installation set, exposes the Step 1 desktop-preview document, and optionally hands control to the native installer.

## Order
1. Locate an existing Git clone.
2. Clone to `$HOME/src/Ubuntu.Determinant.Beta.Restricted` when absent.
3. Locate `installer/install-manifest.txt` or `installer/install-native.sh`.
4. Report `installer/DESKTOP_PREVIEW_STEP_1.md`.
5. Stop safely in dry-run mode.
6. With `--install`, execute the native Linux installer.

## Build
`make`

## Install
`make install`

## Run
`desktop_install_probe`

## Install Mode
`desktop_install_probe --install`

## Safety
Discovery is non-destructive. Installation is explicit. The helper must never claim that installation succeeded when the installer returned failure.

## Files
- `desktop_install_probe.c` — implementation
- `desktop_install_probe.h` — constants/interface definitions
- `Makefile` — build/install rules
- `DESKTOP_INSTALL_PROBE.md` — quick reference
